<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Neo-Elamite kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1000 BCE – 539 BCE (approx.) · capital Susa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last phase of Elam, a determined enemy of Assyria that was crushed by Ashurbanipal but passed its scribal culture on to the Persians.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After a dark period following the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/middle-elamite-kingdom">Middle Elamite kingdom</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> reappears in the 8th century BCE as a kingdom centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a> and the highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzestan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a>. Its kings sought to resist the expanding <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a>, often by backing Babylonian rebels.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humban-nikash-i">Humban-nikash I</a> fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a> at Der in 720 BCE, and Elamite armies supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merodach-baladan-ii">Merodach-baladan</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bit-yakin">Bit-Yakin</a> and fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sennacherib">Sennacherib</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-halule">Halule</a> in 691 BCE. Internal rivalries, often exploited by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>, produced frequent coups. Elamite religion centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inshushinak">Inshushinak</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a>. Assyrian reliefs at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a> show the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ulai">Battle of Til-Tuba</a> in 653 BCE, where King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teumman">Teumman</a> was beheaded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashurbanipal">Ashurbanipal</a> sacked Susa around 646 BCE, desecrating royal tombs and temples. Smaller Neo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite kingdoms</a> survived until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a> absorbed them into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> around 539 BCE. Elamite remained an administrative language of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a>, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persepolis">Persepolis</a> tablets show.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1000 BCE – 539 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesopotamia and Iran</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:39.80%;width:9.17%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1000 BCE – 539 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Susa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Humban-nikash I, Shutruk-Nahhunte II, Teumman</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Elamite religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Elamite</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Neo-Elamite Elam</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-770&amp;focus=neo-elamite-kingdom" aria-label="Neo-Elamite kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5921 1007 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Neo-Elamite kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M62